;; Babashka config for Clojure-native developer and differential tooling.
;; ClojureWasm itself remains a Zig project; bb supervises processes that cljw
;; cannot spawn and shares protocol/domain namespaces with cljw through .cljc.
;;
;; `scripts` is on the path so `scripts/dev/*.cljc` resolves the same way under
;; bb as it does under cljw (`cljw -cp scripts`), which is what lets the nREPL
;; client be ONE implementation shared by both runtimes.
{:paths ["scripts"]}
